  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.15,
      "end": 1.947,
      "text": "That famous black hole image?",
      "beat": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 1.947,
      "end": 4.735,
      "text": "The dark circle is not the black hole itself.",
      "beat": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 4.915,
      "end": 5.876,
      "text": "It is a shadow,",
      "beat": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 5.876,
      "end": 10.679,
      "text": "created by gravity bending the paths of light around an invisible boundary.",
      "beat": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 10.859,
      "end": 13.731,
      "text": "In 2019, scientists revealed the first image:",
      "beat": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 13.731,
      "end": 19.667,
      "text": "a monster at the heart of galaxy M eighty seven, roughly fifty five million light years away.",
      "beat": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 19.847,
      "end": 22.626,
      "text": "Its mass is about six and a half billion Suns.",
      "beat": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 22.626,
      "end": 27.278,
      "text": "The bright ring comes from hot gas around it, not from the black hole itself.",
      "beat": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 27.458,
      "end": 31.159,
      "text": "To see it, astronomers linked radio observatories across Earth,",
      "beat": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 31.159,
      "end": 34.626,
      "text": "creating a virtual telescope nearly the size of our planet.",
      "beat": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 34.806,
      "end": 37.417,
      "text": "This is not a regular camera photograph.",
      "beat": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 37.417,
      "end": 42.118,
      "text": "Computers reconstructed the image from radio observations taken in 2017.",
      "beat": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 42.298,
      "end": 44.957,
      "text": "Beyond the event horizon, light cannot escape.",
      "beat": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 44.957,
      "end": 48.542,
      "text": "But the dark region in the image is larger than that boundary.",
      "beat": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 48.722,
      "end": 53.118,
      "text": "We cannot see the black hole directly. We see what it does to light.",
      "beat": 8
    },
    {
      "start": 53.118,
      "end": 56.092,
      "text": "Save this and subscribe for more real science.",
      "beat": 8
    }
  ]
}